From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bert Belder <bertbelder@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: Allow external code space with multiple pointer compression cages

The Bazel build only enabled the external code space when the shared
pointer compression cage was in use, which in turn disabled the sandbox
and static roots for multi-cage builds. The GN build has no such
restriction: external code space only requires pointer compression, and
V8's own "no shared cage" bot builds with the sandbox and the external
code space enabled. Gate the external code space on pointer compression
alone so that a multi-cage build (v8_enable_pointer_compression_shared_cage
= False) keeps the external code space, static roots and the sandbox.

diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -418,12 +418,12 @@
     default = True,
 )

-# Enable support for external code range if enable_pointer_compression_shared_cage and
-# v8_enable_external_code_space.
+# Enable support for external code range if v8_enable_pointer_compression and
+# v8_enable_external_code_space. This applies to both shared and multiple cages.
 selects.config_setting_group(
     name = "enable_external_code_space",
     match_all = [
-        ":enable_pointer_compression_shared_cage",
+        ":is_v8_enable_pointer_compression",
         ":is_v8_enable_external_code_space",
     ],
 )
